{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Noah knew that the waters had subsided.</b> Since it tarried until evening. And according to the one who says the flood did not descend upon the land of Israel, how did Noah know from the bringing of the leaf that the waters had subsided? He should have been uncertain: perhaps it brought it from the land of Israel, or perhaps it was floating on the face of the waters and it took it. Rather, one may answer: it was evident that it did not bring it from a distant place, for טרף is written — a term of snatching — that it snatched it from the tree, and its snatching testifies about it that had it found it upon the face of the waters, in the manner of other leaves that fall from the tree by wind, it would not have been torn but whole. And likewise the Targum proves it: תביר — snatched in its mouth."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:22.148369716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}